{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1367787-how-do-young-dynasts-try-to-exalt-into-dragon-blooded","id":1367787,"title":"How do young Dynasts TRY to Exalt into Dragon Blooded?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-14T09:16:21-08:00","id":1367787,"title":"How do young Dynasts TRY to Exalt into Dragon Blooded?","content":"The Manuel of Exalted Powers: The Dragon Blooded notes how young Dynasts think of little else but Exalting as one of the Dragon Blooded.<br /> <br /> It notes they try all sorts of ways, some superstitious, to Exalt.<br /> <br /> Obviously they do not have the OOC knowledge of how DB Exaltation work, but the book is also vague about what these young Dynasts <b>THINK </b>will result in Exaltation.<br /> <br /> Has this info been shared in any other books, or a part of that book I missed?<br /> <br /> What kind of practices, acts, or spiritual states do you think these young people might think will prove their worth as a member of the Dragon Blooded host?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T09:18:40-08:00","id":1367788,"title":"","content":"Read the first issue of My Hero Academia and watch little Izuku try to figure out what his Quirk is.<br /> <br /> I imagine there's a LOT of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T09:31:11-08:00","id":1367791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1367787-how-do-young-dynasts-try-to-exalt-into-dragon-blooded?p=1367788#post1367788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Read the first issue of My Hero Academia and watch little Izuku try to figure out what his Quirk is.<br /> <br /> I imagine there's a LOT of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does crying a lot help becoming en Exalted ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T10:05:11-08:00","id":1367797,"title":"","content":"Doesn't the Deeb Exaltation tend to come out under duress? I imagine there's a couple of very stressful years at whatever font of education young dynasts spend their time at, but if they don't flame on by say... 18? maybe the instructors then let nature take it's course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T10:13:20-08:00","id":1367799,"title":"","content":"Travel with a group of their friends out into the woods to see a dead body while facing struggles and growing as people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T10:23:19-08:00","id":1367806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1367787-how-do-young-dynasts-try-to-exalt-into-dragon-blooded#post1367787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of practices, acts, or spiritual states do you think these young people might think will prove their worth as a member of the Dragon Blooded host?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd guess a lot of practices involve contact or immersion in a dangerous amount of the element you expect to have as your Aspect. So a Dynast from House Memnon might bury herself in gravel and try to hold her breath for as long as possible, someone hoping for Fire Aspect might hold her hand in the flame for as long as she could stand it, a Wood Aspect hopeful might drink barely sub-lethal levels of hemlock, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T11:23:43-08:00","id":1367817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1367787-how-do-young-dynasts-try-to-exalt-into-dragon-blooded?p=1367791#post1367791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does crying a lot help becoming en Exalted ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that the only thing you remember little Izuku doing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T11:51:18-08:00","id":1367823,"title":"","content":"Young Dynasts lives are pretty full of adventure and excitement anyway. They go to incredibly demanding schools that teach academic skills as well as physical training and martial arts. On top of that they\u2019re embroiled in family intrigue and dynastic politics from a pretty young age. They\u2019re also given the incredible privilege of having access to faraway and exotic locations as well as otherwise forbidden knowledge. They probably just try to exalt by doing and being the best at their responsibilities. Or alternatively just laze around doing the bare minimum to get by and assume they\u2019re going to exalt regardless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T13:02:23-08:00","id":1367840,"title":"","content":"Don't need a book when real life's got you covered. If you go to YouTube and search &quot;people getting injured for youtube,&quot; you should be able to find some (really gross) inspiration. Humans do dumb things for a lot less than a chance at superpowers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T14:41:39-08:00","id":1367869,"title":"","content":"Steal Dragonblood hair and make it into amulets to keep under their bed.<br /> Make potions of Dragonblood piss/blood/cum. (Acquiring genuine fluids isn't always easy)<br /> Sleep with Dragonblood.<br /> Try practicing Immaculate Dragon-Fu in the style of their parent or house's element.<br /> Pray at temples a lot.<br /> Go on pilgrimage up the Imperial Mountain.<br /> Submerge themselves, bury themselves, jump into fire, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-14-2020, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T14:50:42-08:00","id":1367871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1367787-how-do-young-dynasts-try-to-exalt-into-dragon-blooded?p=1367840#post1367840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't need a book when real life's got you covered. If you go to YouTube and search &quot;people getting injured for youtube,&quot; you should be able to find some (really gross) inspiration. Humans do dumb things for a lot less than a chance at superpowers.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Hi I'm Cathak Knoxville and welcome to Jackass!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T17:09:37-08:00","id":1367929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1367787-how-do-young-dynasts-try-to-exalt-into-dragon-blooded#post1367787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the book is also vague about what these young Dynasts <b>THINK </b>will result in Exaltation</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say vague so much as space that we're invited to fill in for ourselves because there's only so much wordcount.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has this info been shared in any other books, or a part of that book I missed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think some of the Aspect books might have characters describe their experience of such in school, but nothing prominent. There are a few things to the culture of the Scarlet Dynasty.<br /> <br /> I think there's value in having something open-ended for people using the books, but if they ever actually went ahead with a Scarlet Manual of Upright Bearing I think there's a fair amount that it could be filled with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of practices, acts, or spiritual states do you think these young people might think will prove their worth as a member of the Dragon Blooded host?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you can never go wrong with drinking a bit of mercury.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, have them wear a piece of ceremonial clothing from each of the Aspects. Then in a bowl before them, combine the five elements together as one! A jug of water! A cup of soil! A lit torch! Air from a bellows! A pointed stick.<br /> <br /> Scatter the contents over the prospective dragon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T17:21:05-08:00","id":1367930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Young Dynasts lives are pretty full of adventure and excitement anyway. They go to incredibly demanding schools that teach academic skills as well as physical training and martial arts. On top of that they\u2019re embroiled in family intrigue and dynastic politics from a pretty young age.</span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><br /> <br /> The tone that the book seems to present is that Dynast academia is still highly regimented and routine (certainly challenging, but not necessarily exciting), and that family intrigue and politics is something that they're isolated from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They\u2019re also given the incredible privilege of having access to faraway and exotic locations</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe occasionally as a school trip, but that's not definitive and still liable to be strictly supervised.<br /> <br /> The whole point of their post-graduation sabbatical is being the first opportunity to really go out on their own and see the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">just laze around doing the bare minimum to get by and assume they\u2019re going to exalt regardless</div> </div> </div> </div>Hesiesh help the poor young Dynast who takes that attitude to schooling the first time somebody points out the exceptionally well-bred 14-year old mortal who is going to graduate next year. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine there's a couple of very stressful years at whatever font of education young dynasts spend their time at</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but this thread is specifically about the explicitly described practice of weird and futile rituals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">if they don't flame on by say... 18</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine that if they're not Exalted by the time a secondary school is being selected four years prior to that, anxiety levels are going to start shooting through the roof.</span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T19:51:31-08:00","id":1367960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1367787-how-do-young-dynasts-try-to-exalt-into-dragon-blooded?p=1367930#post1367930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe occasionally as a school trip, but that's not definitive and still liable to be strictly supervised.<br /> <br /> The whole point of their post-graduation sabbatical is being the first opportunity to really go out on their own and see the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exotic was probably not the right word. I was more thinking about how some primary schools have naval exercises, or have extreme architecture or landscape, or yes field trips to satrapies. If your school looks like <a href=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/d0/af/86/d0af8681bad4324690a779ffc4cec26b.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> or <a href=\"https://www.bestfunforall.com/better/imgs/Fantasy%20monastery%20wallpaper%20%201.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> or <a href=\"https://wallpaperaccess.com/full/108868.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>, there's plenty of opportunity just in the environment for crazy shit to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T20:12:31-08:00","id":1367962,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking there'd be some milage to trying to emulate the capabilities of the anima banners, like a Tepet jumping from a high place.<br /> <br /> Still, ought to come up with something really weird... Wizard has the right idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T20:16:09-08:00","id":1367963,"title":"","content":"Horrible implications for most aspects there. Burn yourself, if you are chosen of Fire you will exalt and be unburned. Stay under water as long as you can, either drown or become exalted of water. Consume this horrible poison plant and exalt wood to save yourself. Or just jump off this building and Mela will catch you if you're worthy.<br /> <br /> Made all the worse by that being exactly how it works at least some of the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T22:09:43-08:00","id":1367983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1367787-how-do-young-dynasts-try-to-exalt-into-dragon-blooded?p=1367963#post1367963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Horrible implications for most aspects there. Burn yourself, if you are chosen of Fire you will exalt and be unburned. Stay under water as long as you can, either drown or become exalted of water. Consume this horrible poison plant and exalt wood to save yourself. Or just jump off this building and Mela will catch you if you're worthy.<br /> <br /> Made all the worse by that being exactly how it works at least some of the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>And because, well, sometimes the alternative (failure to exalt) is just worse than death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T22:18:22-08:00","id":1367985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1367787-how-do-young-dynasts-try-to-exalt-into-dragon-blooded?p=1367983#post1367983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And because, well, sometimes the alternative (failure to exalt) is just worse than death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, true enough. Somebody at my sister's university set themselves on fire because they couldn't take the pressure anymore, and I'm pretty sure he didn't even consider exaltation an option. Mental health is important guys.<br /> <br /> He lived, just for the record, thanks to the quick action of a other resident and two police officers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-14T22:40:52-08:00","id":1367990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1367787-how-do-young-dynasts-try-to-exalt-into-dragon-blooded?p=1367985#post1367985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, true enough. Somebody at my sister's university set themselves on fire because they couldn't take the pressure anymore, and I'm pretty sure he didn't even consider exaltation an option. Mental health is important guys.<br /> <br /> He lived, just for the record, thanks to the quick action of a other resident and two police officers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Especially when the prize (or so you think) is demigodhood. <br /> <br /> Imagine being set in a culture where superheroes/ demigods were real. Several of your relatives are one. You were told that you might become one, if the Dragons judged you good enough. You worship them, since you were born. You've heard stories about them. Your very religion praises them as the pinnacle of humanity. You wish to be them. <br /> <br /> What to do, when you realize that your dream of demigod-hood might turn out to not be true? What happens when you realise that your childhood dreams will never be true, that you might simply be left as a mortal, shuffled off as an embarassment to family, left to die in less than a hundred years, never making anything of yourself, stuck doing mundane work while your brothers and sisters live the high life, fight behemoths and Fair Folk, and basically living out the life of legends? <br /> <br /> Death might seem to be preferable to failure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-19T19:30:42-07:00","id":1524299,"title":"","content":"I think there are likely several anime out there about young teens doing dangerous things to awaken their super secret inner power. I agree with the sentiment that Dynasts have lots of exposure, however, the longest the exaltation does NOT happen, the more desperate the young dynast will be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-07T15:38:40-08:00","id":1528182,"title":"","content":"Eventually you get something out of a downright nightmarish parody of a given episode of Jackass. Except instead of being horrified and angry at the affair, Bam's mom is pressuring him to go back into the locked up Barn with the King Cobra as tall as he is, so he can be like Daddy and make her proud. And he may be a lot younger. And the survivors then go on to be told how righteous and powerful and godly they are, subtextually because they were abused and became powerful. Heaven help the poor soul who says that last quiet part out loud, however. Probably a few dozen DBs who just straight up avoid the Realm's dating scene because the thought of putting their kids through what they were put through is abhorrent to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-13T04:56:25-08:00","id":1528479,"title":"","content":"I seem to remember that in the Aspect books several superstitions were mentioned about things that made it more likely to exalt. I don't remember which ones exactly, but I do remember that there was an idea, that being close to a Dragon-Blooded increased the chances of exaltation, so many students approached to those that had already exalted in the hope that it would &quot;stick&quot; so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25189-dagurasu","name":"Dagurasu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T21:31:28-08:00","id":1529065,"title":"","content":"I have the Realm have a law against disseminating any such methods; over the years too many have died trying these things out. Although there is a carve out in the law; the Caul Pilgrimage is exempt and therefore is the closest thing to an official way to 'sway the Dragons&quot;. <br /> But various potions, feats of strength/endurance, fasting, prayers and more were all tried.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}